  "cardinality_note": "Both estimators now charge a flat 10 guesses per unexplained character, so they differ in their lexicon and not in this. The observed_cardinality arm restores the classical alphabet-size model (26/36/95) that IndicPass shipped with in Milestone 1: it was responsible for essentially the whole divergence from the baseline on random controls, where there is no lexical structure to find and therefore nothing the Indic dictionary could have contributed."
